---
/**
 * Diagram 4 — research, plan, code, verify, drawn as a loop.
 *
 * The four stages run left to right because that is the order you walk them
 * the first time. What makes it a loop rather than a line is the two return
 * arcs underneath, and those are the only labelled edges in the drawing:
 * verifying almost always sends you back to the code, and sometimes all the
 * way back to the plan. The short arc carries the accent because it is the
 * one you travel most.
 *
 * Theming and sizing: see StackDiagram.astro. Ids are prefixed `bl-`.
 */
---

<figure class="qu-diagram">
	<svg
		viewBox="0 0 440 156"
		role="img"
		aria-labelledby="bl-title bl-desc"
		xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
	>
		<title id="bl-title">Research, plan, code, verify — drawn as a loop, not a line</title>
		<desc id="bl-desc">
			Four boxes in a row, joined left to right by arrows: Research, then Plan,
			then Code, then Verify. Two arcs run back underneath from Verify. The
			first and shorter arc, highlighted, returns to Code and is labelled fix
			and re-verify. The second and longer arc returns all the way to Plan and
			is labelled back to the plan, if the plan was wrong.
		</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker
				id="bl-arrow"
				markerWidth="9"
				markerHeight="7"
				refX="8"
				refY="3.5"
				orient="auto"
				markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
			>
				<path class="head" d="M0 0 L9 3.5 L0 7 Z" />
			</marker>
			<marker
				id="bl-arrow-accent"
				markerWidth="9"
				markerHeight="7"
				refX="8"
				refY="3.5"
				orient="auto"
				markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
			>
				<path class="head-accent" d="M0 0 L9 3.5 L0 7 Z" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<rect class="box" x="3" y="26" width="89" height="40" rx="8" />
		<text class="name mid" x="47.5" y="51">Research</text>

		<rect class="box" x="118" y="26" width="89" height="40" rx="8" />
		<text class="name mid" x="162.5" y="51">Plan</text>

		<rect class="box" x="233" y="26" width="89" height="40" rx="8" />
		<text class="name mid" x="277.5" y="51">Code</text>

		<rect class="box" x="348" y="26" width="89" height="40" rx="8" />
		<text class="name mid" x="392.5" y="51">Verify</text>

		<line class="flow" x1="92" y1="46" x2="114" y2="46" marker-end="url(#bl-arrow)" />
		<line class="flow" x1="207" y1="46" x2="229" y2="46" marker-end="url(#bl-arrow)" />
		<line class="flow" x1="322" y1="46" x2="344" y2="46" marker-end="url(#bl-arrow)" />

		<path
			class="flow accent"
			d="M392.5 68 L392.5 98 Q392.5 104 386.5 104 L283.5 104 Q277.5 104 277.5 98 L277.5 72"
			marker-end="url(#bl-arrow-accent)"
		/>
		<text class="step mid lead" x="335" y="92">fix and re-verify</text>

		<path
			class="flow"
			d="M415 68 L415 134 Q415 140 409 140 L168.5 140 Q162.5 140 162.5 134 L162.5 72"
			marker-end="url(#bl-arrow)"
		/>
		<text class="step mid" x="289" y="130">back to the plan, if the plan was wrong</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		The arrows that matter are the ones pointing backwards. Nothing here is
		specific to AI — it is the loop every working engineer already runs.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.qu-diagram {
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.qu-diagram svg {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 27.5rem;
		height: auto;
		margin-inline: auto;
		font-family: var(--sl-font);
	}

	.qu-diagram figcaption {
		margin: 0.875rem auto 0;
		max-width: 27.5rem;
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	.box {
		fill: var(--sl-color-bg-sidebar);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-hairline);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}

	.flow {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1.25;
	}

	.head {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	/* One accented edge: the return you actually travel every time. */
	.accent {
		stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}

	.head-accent {
		fill: var(--sl-color-accent);
	}

	.name {
		fill: var(--sl-color-white);
		font-size: 14px;
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.step {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		font-size: 12px;
	}

	/*
	 * Declared after .step so its fill wins on source order. Ink and medium
	 * weight, not jade: accent text would read as a link, and the arc beside
	 * it is already carrying the accent.
	 */
	.lead {
		fill: var(--sl-color-white);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.mid {
		text-anchor: middle;
	}
</style>
